# `"s".nonexistent_member_xyz()` reached Roslyn and came back as CS1061 behind SPY0908 — the
# compiler reporting its own bug for a typo (#1291). Reflection can PROVE the member absent on a
# builtin receiver, and where it can, the refusal is Sharpy's own.
#
# BuiltinType receivers ONLY. The same fall-through carries GenericType and TupleType receivers whose
# members codegen resolves through discovery paths the absence proof does not model, and a false
# refusal rejects a working program — worse than the ICE it replaces. The twin below is the
# measurement of that: raw BCL spellings on a builtin receiver still bind.


def main() -> None:
    s = "abc"
    print(s.nonexistent_member_xyz())
